    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{n}$",
      "worked": "Cancel the common factors $2,3,\\ldots,n-1$ in the numerator and denominator.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2}\\times\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{3}{4}\\times\\cdots\\frac{n-1}{n}&=\\frac{1\\times2\\times3\\times\\cdots\\times(n-1)}{2\\times3\\times4\\times\\cdots\\times n}\\\\&=\\frac{1}{n}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 29
